<title>JAPAN: Chinon shares bid-only on restructuring plan.</title>
<headline>Chinon shares bid-only on restructuring plan.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Chinon Industries Inc were bid-only on Friday morning, following news on Thursday that Eastman Kodak and Hachijuni Bank Ltd had agreed to support Chinon's restructuring efforts turning Eastman Kodak into a majority shareholder.</p>
<p>The share price of the video camera lense maker was bid-only at 259 yen, above its Thursday's 234 yen.  </p>
<p>Under the restructuring program, Chinon will allocate 9.91 million new shares worth 1.88 billion yen to Eastman Kodak and its group companies.</p>
<p>Kodak is already the top shareholder of Chinon, with a 12.18 percent stake. The new allocation will raise that to 50.1 percent, Chinon said.</p>
</text>
